{"id":"a8d6de2f-bb06-4bf3-95d3-c93709e4c6f1","object":"chat.completion","created":1784994424,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    word_token_indices = case['word_token_indices']\\n    word_labels = case['word_labels']\\n    token_count = case['token_count']\\n    \\n    if len(word_token_indices) != len(word_labels):\\n        raise ValueError('Mismatch between number of word groups and word labels')\\n    \\n    token_labels = [None] * token_count\\n    used = set()\\n    \\n    for i, idx_list in enumerate(word_token_indices):\\n        label = word_labels[i]\\n        for idx in idx_list:\\n            if not isinstance(idx, int) or idx < 0 or idx >= token_count:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Token index {idx} out of range')\\n            if idx in used:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Duplicate token index {idx}')\\n            used.add(idx)\\n            token_labels[idx] = label\\n    \\n    if len(used) != token_count:\\n        missing = set(range(token_count)) - used\\n        raise ValueError(f'Uncovered token indices: {missing}')\\n    \\n    # Convert to list of ints (None should not happen)\\n    token_labels = [label for label in token_labels]\\n    kept_indices = [i for i, label in enumerate(token_labels) if label == 1]\\n    \\n    return {'kept_indices': kept_indices, 'token_labels': token_labels}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task NLP-LL2-01. The payload has fields: word_token_indices (list of lists of ints), word_labels (list of ints), token_count (int), _case_nonce (string). We must output object with kept_indices (array of ints) and token_labels (array of ints).\n\nProcess: Iterate over each word group (i-th word). For each token index in word_token_indices[i], assign the label from word_labels[i] to that token position. We need to validate: no overlapping indices across word groups, all indices within 0..token_count-1, and every token index from 0 to token_count-1 must appear exactly once? Actually requirement says \"Reject overlapping, out-of-range, or uncovered token indices.\" So the union of all token indices across all words must be exactly the set {0,...,token_count-1} and no duplicates. Also each word must have at least one token? The description \"Require one word label for every registered word group.\" Means each word group has a label. So word_labels length must equal word_token_indices length. Also each word must have at least one token? Possibly but not explicitly required. But if a word has empty token list, that might be allowed? Usually not. We'll assume non-empty.\n\nImplementation: \n- Validate that len(word_token_indices) == len(word_labels)\n- Create an array token_labels of size token_count, initialized to None or placeholder.\n- Create a set of used indices.\n- For each word i, for each token idx in word_token_indices[i]:\n   - Check idx is integer, 0 <= idx < token_count\n   - If idx already in used set: raise ValueError (overlap)\n   - Set token_labels[idx] = word_labels[i]\n   - Add idx to used set.\n- After processing all words, check that used set covers all indices 0..token_count-1. If any missing: raise ValueError.\n- Then kept_indices: list of indices where token_labels[idx] == 1.\n- Return {\"kept_indices\": kept_indices, \"token_labels\": token_labels}\n\nNote: token_labels must be list of ints (0 or 1). We'll ensure that all labels are 0 or 1? The input word_labels are given as integers. The requirement says \"keep token indices whose broadcast label equals one.\" So labels can be 0 or 1. If word_labels contain other values, maybe treat 1 as keep, others as drop? But specification says \"word_labels\" list of integers. We'll assume valid.\n\nEdge cases: nonce is not used in computation.\n\nNow produce code. Must be Python source string inside JSON implementation key.\n\nPotential pitfalls: The output must exactly match schema: integer arrays. Use list comprehensions.\n\nWrite solve(case) function. Include ValueError for invalid cases.\n\nReturn the JSON object with \"implementation\". Use json.dumps on the Python string.\n\nLet's produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1239,"completion_tokens":958,"total_tokens":2197,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":629},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":87},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}